  "architecture_review": [
    "One immutable stdlib-only canonical plan lives in existing standalone transport.py. Producer imports BASE/MODERN/SELECTED tuples from its verified source root; old selected18 values are byte-semantic equivalents, not a second registry.",
    "consumer_layout is pure in-memory projection returning nested tuples; exact Git roots and image paths are frozen sets. Pack and verify compute the trusted plan, rather than accepting report/manifest lists as authorization.",
    "Producer base/modern/selected loops retain original commands, order, toolchain selection, source identity, build parallel argument and resource/retention/runtime checks. No producer execution was removed.",
    "Standalone pack/verify has only stdlib imports; attach retains its existing explicit source policy import. Transport does not import consumer builder or arbitrary raw-output modules.",
    "Current schema_version is strictly int2; policy is nexus-sdk-consumers-v2; exact root/image claims and raw_bytes_pruned=False are mandatory. Historical schema1/old13 stays frozen and is rejected as a current fallback.",
    "Existing strict Git skeleton checks remain: exact root set, only unborn HEAD/core defaults/comment excludes/default description/sample hooks and empty allowed subdirectories; files named .git, history/index/refs/logs/remotes/active hooks/foreign metadata remain rejected.",
    "No symlink/hardlink/special member, safe-name, duplicate JSON/member, nonempty owned fresh-separated output, MAX_FILES/MAX_BYTES and original raw byte/SHA/file-mode inventory checks were weakened.",
    "Original verification.json bytes equal the raw archive member; source and builder/run/workflow/helper identities remain separate. Transport validates claims and retains logs; it does not prove a command actually ran.",
    "package_source_sdk.py adds transport.py explicitly to REQUIRED_FILES. Real SDK verify rejects its rehashed omission before later dependency admission; default export alone is not used as proof.",
    "No CI required-job set, workflow YAML, release gate, source policy, SDK locks, tool/dependency identity or firmware source changed."
  ],
